# A card visibly counted down in exile. Ancestral Vision ({U}, Suspend
# 3—{1}{U}) sits in seat 0's exile zone with three TIME counters already on
# it, scripted directly rather than cast: `GameState.java:427-431` supports
# counters in Exile the same way it does on the battlefield, and Ancestral
# Vision's own printed Suspend keyword is what makes `Card.hasSuspend()` true
# the moment the card is in Exile with at least one TIME counter
# (`Card.java:1703`) — nothing about suspend itself needs scripting, only the
# zone and the counters.
#
# Lands DIRECTLY at seat 0's own Upkeep with `activephase` (a JUMP: "no
# phase-begin/end effects run" — scenarios/README.md), not
# `activephaseadvance` — so Suspend's own upkeep trigger has NOT fired yet
# and the count is still 3 the instant a client ever sees this match, no race
# against the server's own auto-pass possible (measured: with the OTHER
# shape, landing one phase short and letting the ordinary loop walk into
# Upkeep, the trigger had already fired — counter already 2 — before a
# client-driven check ever ran). From here the ordinary game loop walks
# forward exactly once (Draw, Main 1, combat, Main 2, End, Cleanup, the
# opponent's whole turn, Untap) into the SECOND Upkeep, a real
# `activephaseadvance`-shaped walk this time, where the trigger fires for
# real and removes one counter.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=UPKEEP
